# --- Voice engines: swappable text-to-speech -------------------------------
# Everything above synthesize() is engine-agnostic, so the engine can be
# changed from the settings panel mid-flight. See voice-messages.md.
#
#   ha        Home Assistant tts.speak / assist_satellite announce. Speaks on
#             the Pine Box. Produces no audio file.
#   piper     Wyoming Piper directly (tcp 10200) -> a WAV at /media/<key>.
#   ha_file   Home Assistant tts_get_url -> the finished file at /media/<key>.
#   browser   The browser's own speechSynthesis. No file, device voices only
#             (voice-messages.md 3.3) — kept as the no-server fallback.
#   xtts      XTTS v2 clone server on the host (:8770) — zero-shot cloning
#             from a reference wav in the voice library (data/voices). The
#             voice is a library id (vl_*), not a Piper name.
